Rewrite FUN_1000_1467 (MEMMGR pool/free-list builder) with FAITHFUL dynamic-DS CHAIN tracking.

After INT 21h AH=48, FUN_1000_140e hands the new block segment (param_1, e.g. 0x3400) to 1467, which
seeds a block header at ES:0 (ES pinned = block base) and then threads a doubly-linked circular
free-list of fixed-size node paragraphs, WALKING DS through block, block+2, block+4, ... via
`mov ds,ax; add ax,2` and a `loop`. The previous patch 013 pinned DS=param_1 for the WHOLE function,
so every per-node write landed on the block header itself: the free list was never built, block[0x0a]
(the list head FUN_1000_096c reads) stayed 0, and the free-list walker crashed dereferencing a null
node segment. This version tracks DS instruction-by-instruction from the asm (base-0 0x11467..0x115f3).
Class: docs/stage1.md "dynamic-DS loop-updated segment" (SegmentFixup handles DS=CS only, not the
DS=<register-updated-per-node> idiom). Registers: param_1=block seg (AX->DS,ES), param_2=alignment (CX),
param_3=size (BX). Verified at runtime: block[0x0a] = block+2 (valid free-list head) after this patch.

